      "writtenOn": "2017-10-10T03:43:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not for this change, but... do we impose no limits on key lenghts? Shouldn\u0027t we? For example, it seems clearly invalid to have an empty key, or a key that\u0027s only 8 bits long...",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 119,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "fb8b4468f1736119aeba5187daedebee5393289b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1384d2d_6e88ce10",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/IpSecAlgorithm.java",
        "patchSetId": 35
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-10T19:20:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIK, the kernel will throw an EINVAL on an invalid key length; I can file a bug to track this, and investigate further.\n\nb/67638246",
      "parentUuid": "bdab9319_360110c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 119,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "fb8b4468f1736119aeba5187daedebee5393289b",
