    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53a1cb24_4b006c48",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/IpSecAlgorithm.java",
        "patchSetId": 35
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-18T05:04:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I assume it will. Should we rely on the kernel to tell us what\u0027s wrong? If so, should we remove some of the checks int the service, such as the one that checks that AEAD is not simultaneously used with auth or crypto? I assume the kernel will return EINVAL if ask it to do that, right?\n\nHaving security checks spread across two places can sometimes result in confusion and security vulnerabilities (e.g., if both components think that the other component is responsible for checking for a particular condition).",
      "parentUuid": "a1384d2d_6e88ce10",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 119,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "fb8b4468f1736119aeba5187daedebee5393289b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
